hi this is presh talwalkar let's discuss  a math problem from the movie little man  tate  the problem is you need to find a number  that when divided by the product of its  digits you get an answer of 3 and when  you add 18 to the number the digits of  the number are reversed  the problem is difficult to set up  because it involves the actual digits in  the number  so to figure out how we can do this  we'll do a refresher  when you have the number 12  that really means 10 times 1 plus 2  and if you have the number 58 that means  10 times 5 plus 8.  so in general if you have a number xy in  the decimal system that's 10 times x  plus y  we can use this to set up the first  problem that when you take the number  and divide it by its product of the  digits you get the quotient of 3.  the other condition is when you add 18  to the number you reverse the digits x  and y  this implies that y equals x plus 2  which we're going to substitute into our  other condition  we end up with a quadratic equation  which we can factor out  and at this point we can get to the  solution of x equals minus 1 3 or x  equals 2. obviously the digits have to  be positive so we have x equals 2.  we substitute that back in to find y  equals 4 and we have the answer of 24  we can look at the problem again and  we'll verify that this indeed is a  solution when we divide it by the  product of the digits we get 3 and when  we add 18 the digits are reversed please  subscribe to my channel  you can support me on patreon  you can catch me on my blog  binderdecisions on twitter at  preshtalocker  and you can get my books and amazon
 

